    "Provider to confirm the 29 April visit and the attending company (Riverside Compliance or Cedar Utilities).",
    "Record the visit outcome after 29 April (follow-up FUP-103 set for 2026-04-29).",
    "If a repair or quote is needed, obtain the landlord's recorded decision before instructing work. No landlord words are on file for a repair spend; the agency note 'LL already agreed for GS to go out' (event 008) is not a quoted landlord decision.",
    "Confirm the landlord's name and approval record for this property: get_property returned no landlord details or spend limit."
  ],
  "missing_info": [
    "Provider confirmation of the 29 April visit (the only confirmation on file is the system record and the agency's own message).",
    "Landlord's recorded decision for any repair beyond inspection; no spend limit on file for the property.",
    "Identity of 'Imogen Oakley' in event 012 and whether the landlord was asked about the repair directly."
  ],
  "outcome": "action_taken",
  "severity": "routine",
  "summary": "The dishwasher door repair is at the visit stage, with a provider visit recorded for 29 April 2026 (8am-12pm). Leo Turner reported on 28 April that the door still won't close, so I replied to him on the existing thread confirming the booked visit, and asked Riverside Compliance to confirm the date and which company is attending, with a review on 29 April.",
