    {
      "question": "Where does this case stand right now, and what is outstanding?",
      "answer": "At visit stage. Visit recorded for 29/04/2026 08:00 (event 017, sent to tenant and provider). Tenant says the fault persists (event 021). Outstanding: provider confirmation of the visit and the attending company, the visit outcome, and any quote and landlord approval if a repair is needed."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the next action, who is it for, and through which channel?",
      "answer": "Email the tenant Leo Turner (existing thread, event 021) to confirm the booked visit, and email Riverside Compliance (existing thread, event 015) to confirm the visit and attending company. Review on 2026-04-29 to record the outcome (FUP-103)."
    },
    {
      "question": "Does anything need a human decision, and why?",
      "answer": "No escalation now. The routine steps are in hand. A landlord decision will be needed only if a repair or quote follows the visit, and that is a request to the landlord, not an escalation at this stage."
    }
  ],
  "actions_claimed": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "A1",
      "description": "Email to tenant Leo Turner confirming the 29 April visit is being confirmed with the provider"
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A2",
      "description": "Email to Riverside Compliance asking them to confirm the 29 April visit and attending company"
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A3",
      "description": "Follow-up FUP-103 set for 2026-04-29 to review the visit outcome"
    }
  ],
  "failed_actions": [],
  "conflicts": [
    "Event 016 says the caller was 'Grant from Cedar Utilities' and calls the tenant 'Leo Kendall'; the provider on record is Riverside Compliance and the tenant is Leo Turner. Trusted the system assignment and the tenant name in events 015 and 018; asked the provider to confirm.",
    "Event 020 SMS is signed 'Harbour Homes' and gives a different number (07700 900410) from the one in event 015 (07700 900763, which is the tenant's number). Trusted the provider contact on the job record (event 019).",
    "Event 016 says 'this Wednesday between 8 and 12' while event 017 records 08:00. Both point to Wednesday 29 April; the window is 8am-12pm."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The 29 April visit is treated as booked because the system recorded it (event 017) and the tenant and provider were sent the details. This has not been confirmed by the provider.",
    "Event 008 ('LL already agreed for GS to go out') and event 012 are agency notes, not quoted landlord words, so they do not count as a repair spend approval."
  ]
}

